{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If the length of data is not a multiple of size, the final partial chunk is yielded.\n    If size is larger than the length of data, a single chunk containing all data is yielded.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes or list): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: List of chunks of data.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Chunk size must be positive\")\n    if not data:\n        return []\n    chunks = []\n    for i in range(0, len(data), size):\n        chunks.append(data[i:i + size])\n    return chunks\n","expected_sha256":"ceec9407e1f1c99105330d79cb54066072743ddb243713c82223ffcd4133bace","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"Changed chunk to return a list of chunks instead of a generator to match expected output in tests. Added explicit ValueError raise for non-positive size. Return empty list for empty data to satisfy tests expecting list, not generator. This preserves the public API (function signature) and satisfies all acceptance criteria."}